# LLM Server Configuration
# The llama-server URL (without trailing slash)
# Example: http://192.168.x.x:8080
LLAMA_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Shield proxy URL — required by loadgen/run_comparison.sh (the "defense-on" leg of
# the interleaved on/off comparison). Not read by the shield itself (it binds its own
# port via SHIELD_PORT below); this is where load generators send defense-on traffic.
# SHIELD_URL=http://192.168.x.x:9090

# Optional: port the Shield proxy listens on (defaults to 9090)
# SHIELD_PORT=9090

# Optional: SHIELD_ACTIVE=false makes the Shield a pure pass-through logger
# (Day-1 behavior in CLAUDE.md) instead of enforcing admission control.
# SHIELD_ACTIVE=true

# REQUIRED to be kept in sync manually: must equal the -np value service/start.sh
# actually passes to llama-server. The Shield has no way to read llama-server's
# real -np at runtime. If this drifts from the real value, slot reservation
# (Defense C, concurrency layer) silently over- or under-reserves — no error, it
# just stops doing what it's supposed to. Whoever changes NUM_PARALLEL in
# service/start.sh must update this too.
# TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS=4

# Optional: fraction of TOTAL_LLAMA_SLOTS reserved exclusively for legitimate-tier
# in-flight requests (default 0.5)
# LEGITIMATE_SLOT_FRACTION=0.5

# Optional: cache TTL (seconds) for the Shield's /slots availability check
# (default 0.5). Added after a Phase 3 flood test theorized that a fresh,
# uncached /slots round trip on every single incoming request was itself
# contributing to Shield-side timeouts under heavy load — see
# docs/MANUAL_CONFIG.md. UNVERIFIED as of the fix; tune once real rerun data
# exists rather than guessing a "better" number now.
# SLOT_CHECK_TTL=0.5

# Optional: Prometheus scrape endpoint (if monitoring llama-server metrics)
# PROMETHEUS_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.x.x:8080/metrics
